namespace UObjectToolTips

DreamShaderSettings:bEnableDreamMCPEndpoint {
    at    Source/DreamShader/Public/DreamShaderSettings.h#DreamShaderSettings:bEnableDreamMCPEndpoint
    src   "When enabled, the editor serves DreamShader to a DreamMCP server (an MCP server that lets an AI agent check, compile and preview sources) over HTTP on 127.0.0.1 only, behind a token written to Saved/DreamMCP/shader.json. Disable it to keep the editor from listening at all; -NoDreamMCP on the command line does the same for one session. Takes effect the next time the editor starts. The DreamShaderHost commandlet a DreamMCP server starts when no editor is open is not affected."
}

DreamShaderSettings:bScanPluginSourceDirectories {
    at    Source/DreamShader/Public/DreamShaderSettings.h#DreamShaderSettings:bScanPluginSourceDirectories
    src   "When enabled, every enabled plugin that ships a DShader folder contributes its own source root, so a plugin can carry the .dsm/.dsf/.dsh files that build its materials. Plugin roots are discovered and compiled but never rewritten by the editor -- only the project's own source directory is writable. Imports never cross roots: a file resolves its imports against its own root and that root's Packages folder."
}

DreamShaderSettings:bShowEphemeralMaterials {
    at    Source/DreamShader/Public/DreamShaderSettings.h#DreamShaderSettings:bShowEphemeralMaterials
    src   "Applies to the ThinCustom/Instance backend only -- it is the only one with an Ephemeral state, which it hides via UDreamShaderMaterialInstance::IsAsset. When enabled, Ephemeral materials appear in the Content Browser like unsaved assets. Disabled by default: the source files are the intended authoring surface, and hiding the materials also prevents accidental Save actions from materializing them to disk. Graph-backend materials are plain UMaterials with no way to opt out of asset enumeration, so they are always visible and this setting does not affect them."
    text  "仅对 ThinCustom/Instance 后端生效——只有它有 Ephemeral 状态，并用 UDreamShaderMaterialInstance::IsAsset 把它隐藏。启用后，临时材质会像未保存资产一样出现在内容浏览器里。默认关闭：源文件才是预期的编写面板，隐藏材质也能防止误触保存把它们写死到磁盘。Graph 后端的材质是普通 UMaterial，无法退出资产枚举，所以它们始终可见，此设置对它们无效。"
    state machine
}

DreamShaderSettings:bSyncSourceReferencesOnAssetRename {
    at    Source/DreamShader/Public/DreamShaderSettings.h#DreamShaderSettings:bSyncSourceReferencesOnAssetRename
    src   "When enabled, renaming or moving an asset in the editor rewrites the .dsm/.dsf/.dsh files that reference it, so a source keeps naming the asset rather than the path it used to have. Only files under the project source directory are rewritten -- plugin source roots are never touched -- and each file is copied to a .bak next to it before it is written. Batched renames such as Fix Up Redirectors are coalesced into a single pass. Deleting an asset is not covered: a deletion has no new path to write, and the compile error it produces is the correct outcome. Turn this off if you would rather the plugin never edited your source files on its own."
}

DreamShaderSettings:DefaultBackend {
    at    Source/DreamShader/Public/DreamShaderSettings.h#DreamShaderSettings:DefaultBackend
    src   "How DreamShader materializes a source file that does not specify Settings = { Backend = \"...\" }. ThinCustom (the default) builds the material graph on a hidden per-material base and emits a lightweight, Ephemeral material instance of it -- full feature surface, no visible per-material asset. Graph builds a visible UMaterial node graph. Instance is a deprecated alias for ThinCustom."
}

DreamShaderSettings:GraphLayoutStyle {
    at    Source/DreamShader/Public/DreamShaderSettings.h#DreamShaderSettings:GraphLayoutStyle
    src   "How the nodes of a generated graph are placed. Blocks, the default, boxes the graph by region and run of statements, in source order, and lets no wire leave a box: a value another box reads travels through a named reroute, and a constant is repeated where it is read. Source Bands puts one horizontal band per source statement, top to bottom in source order, so the graph reads like the file; Layered draws the whole graph as one layered drawing; those two insert no reroute nodes. These three are computed on the compiler's IR, before any node exists, and are deterministic. Classic is the 1.x layout, which works on the finished graph. Node positions are not part of a generated asset's digest: changing this never makes an asset look hand-edited, and it takes effect the next time a source is rebuilt. `dsc dump-layout` draws the three IR styles of a source as SVG without building anything."
}

DreamShaderSettings:InstanceSubfolder {
    at    Source/DreamShader/Public/DreamShaderSettings.h#DreamShaderSettings:InstanceSubfolder
    src   "Subfolder, relative to the parent material's folder, where the Material Content Browser creates new material instances. Leave empty to create them alongside the parent."
}

DreamShaderSettings:PreprocessorDefines {
    at    Source/DreamShader/Public/DreamShaderSettings.h#DreamShaderSettings:PreprocessorDefines
    src   "Preprocessor defines every .dsm/.dsf/.dsh source compiles with -- what its #if / #elif conditions read. The name answers defined(); a value that parses as an integer compares as a number, anything else as a string; an empty value still counts as defined; a name absent from this table evaluates to 0, as in C. Conditions are evaluated at GENERATION time and the losing branch is cut before the parser sees it, so a condition can select a Domain, a ShadingModel or a whole Outputs block -- none of which a StaticSwitch can reach, because they describe what the material IS rather than what it computes. Editing this table rebuilds only the generated assets whose sources actually read a name that changed. Names are case-sensitive and must match [A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*. The DS_ prefix is reserved for the read-only builtins; an entry using it is dropped with a log warning rather than failing the compile, since a settings mistake has no source line to report against."
}

EDreamShaderDefaultBackend {
    at    Source/DreamShader/Public/DreamShaderSettings.h#EDreamShaderDefaultBackend
    src   "Backend used for source files that do not specify Settings = { Backend = \"...\" } themselves."
    text  "用于未自行指定 `Settings = { Backend = \"...\" }` 的源文件的后端。"
    state machine
}

EDreamShaderDefaultBackend.Graph {
    at    Source/DreamShader/Public/DreamShaderSettings.h#EDreamShaderDefaultBackend:Graph
    src   "Build a UMaterial node graph per material (full DSL feature surface)."
    text  "为每个材质构建 UMaterial 节点图表（DSL 的全部特性）。"
    state machine
}

EDreamShaderDefaultBackend.Instance {
    at    Source/DreamShader/Public/DreamShaderSettings.h#EDreamShaderDefaultBackend:Instance
    src   "DEPRECATED alias for ThinCustom (kept for one deprecation window so existing configs and\nSettings = { Backend = \"Instance\" } sources keep working). The legacy graphless-host instance\nbackend is retired; \"Instance\" now generates the ThinCustom chain."
    text  "ThinCustom 的已弃用别名（保留一个弃用窗口，让既有配置与\n`Settings = { Backend = \"Instance\" }` 的源码继续可用）。旧的无线图表宿主实例\n后端已退役；现在 \"Instance\" 生成的是 ThinCustom 链路。"
    state machine
}

EDreamShaderDefaultBackend.ThinCustom {
    at    Source/DreamShader/Public/DreamShaderSettings.h#EDreamShaderDefaultBackend:ThinCustom
    src   "Build the material graph on a hidden per-material base UMaterial and emit a lightweight\nmaterial instance of it. Full Graph feature surface (the construction is shared) plus the\ninstance's Ephemeral hiding and root shader-map ownership. The default."
    text  "在一个隐藏的每材质基 UMaterial 上构建材质图表，并生成它的轻量\n材质实例。具备 Graph 的全部特性（构建过程共用），再加上\n实例的 Ephemeral 隐藏与根着色器映射归属。默认选项。"
    state machine
}

EDreamShaderGraphLayoutStyle {
    at    Source/DreamShader/Public/DreamShaderSettings.h#EDreamShaderGraphLayoutStyle
    src   "How the nodes of a generated graph are placed. Positions are not part of a generated asset's digest, so switching never makes an asset look hand-edited."
}

EDreamShaderGraphLayoutStyle.Blocks {
    at    Source/DreamShader/Public/DreamShaderSettings.h#EDreamShaderGraphLayoutStyle:Blocks
    src   "One box per `#pragma region` or run of statements, packed in source order like words on a page; no wire leaves a box -- a value another box reads travels through a named reroute, and a constant is repeated. Computed on the IR."
}

EDreamShaderGraphLayoutStyle.Classic {
    at    Source/DreamShader/Public/DreamShaderSettings.h#EDreamShaderGraphLayoutStyle:Classic
    src   "The 1.x layout: blocks recovered from the material's outputs, named reroutes between blocks."
}

EDreamShaderGraphLayoutStyle.Layered {
    at    Source/DreamShader/Public/DreamShaderSettings.h#EDreamShaderGraphLayoutStyle:Layered
    src   "One layered drawing of the whole graph. Computed on the IR, inserts no reroute."
}

EDreamShaderGraphLayoutStyle.SourceBands {
    at    Source/DreamShader/Public/DreamShaderSettings.h#EDreamShaderGraphLayoutStyle:SourceBands
    src   "One horizontal band per source statement, in source order; a `#pragma region` is a box around consecutive bands. Computed on the IR, inserts no reroute."
}

